rence-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An async MCP write tool's library emit fires because the suppression context exited before the awaited handler body executed"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the MCP `suppress_library_double_advisory` proxy must diverge from the established `install_error_guard`/`install_js_safe_guard` `mcp.tool`-rebind idiom (documenting the LLM-tool-exclusion reason), or reshape it to compose with that idiom.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_mcp_errors.py:94-130 rebinds `mcp.tool = guarded_tool` (install idiom); install_js_safe_guard does the same","mcp_server.py:688-693 comment: 'Both rebind mcp.tool and compose.' — the install-guard idiom is the established pattern, called once before registration","The plan's proxy (_SuppressingRegistrar with __getattr__ delegation) is instead applied at two call sites: register_read_tools(suppress...(mcp)) and register_write_tools(suppress...(mcp))","A legitimate divergence exists: register_llm_tools(mcp, ...) is intentionally NOT wrapped, which a globally-installed mcp.tool rebind could not selectively skip"],"finding":"The MCP `suppress_library_double_advisory(mcp)` introduces a new proxy-object registrar pattern for wrapping tool registration, while the codebase already establishes a different idiom for the same job (install_error_guard / install_js_safe_guard rebind `mcp.tool` in place and compose). Two parallel mechanisms for wrap-tool-handler is a cargo-cult/consistency concern worth confirming.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff0beba397b7772d7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Surface layering (MCP bullet); Scope → src/rebar/_lib_warn.py and src/rebar/mcp_server.py","norm_id":"n36a8c5938702ae14","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future maintainer adding a fourth tool-wrapping guard has to choose between two divergent idioms","Composition order between the proxy and the two install-guards is implicit rather than explicit"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Note in the plan that the proxy shape is chosen specifically because LLM tools must be excluded from suppression (which a global `mcp.tool` rebind cannot do); or express suppression as a per-tool decorator applied only on read/write registration to stay closer to the existing guard idiom.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"n